  "body": "### Summary\nAs a reader, I want links to topics and lists to open in the app whatever their slug shape, so that no real forum link is sent to the browser.\n\n### Scope\n`HFRLinkRouteCorpusTests.everyLinkIsAccountedFor` fails on the corpus pages added by PR #474 (R121c, R121e): `HFRLinkRoute.route(for:)` returns `.external` for four real shapes: `/hfr/<cat>/<sub>/sujet_<post>_<page>.htm` (empty title slug, with and without `#bas`), `/hardwarefr/<cat>/sujet-<post>-<page>.htm` (empty slug, hyphen form on the `hardwarefr` prefix) and `/hfr/<cat>/liste_sujet_filtre-<n>-<m>.htm` (filtered list). Route them, or list them as deliberately external with the reason, in the router and its test.\n\n### Acceptance criteria\n- [ ] The four shapes are routed (or exempted with a reason); the corpus test is green.\n- [ ] The exemption in `HFRLinkRouteCorpusTests.isKnownUnroutedView` (\"Real shapes from R121c, R121e\") is removed.\n- [ ] `swift test` green.\n\nRefs #121\n",
